## 349. Intersection of Two Arrays

## Approach - HashSet
--  Store all elements of nums1 in a HashSet.
--  Traverse nums2 and check whether each element exists in the set.
--  If found, add it to the result array.
--  Remove the element from the set after adding it — this prevents duplicates.
--  Since result was initialized with nums2.length, use Arrays.copyOf(result, index) to return only the portion containing valid results.

Note :
Used Arrays.copyOf() to return a new array containing only the valid elements found, instead of the unused zero-filled portion of the original array.

## Complexity
Time: O(n + m) average
Space: O(n) auxiliary space for the HashSet

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public int[] intersection(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {
        HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
        int index = 0;
        for (int i : nums1) {
            set.add(i);
        }
        int[] result = new int[nums2.length];
        for (int i : nums2) {
            if (set.contains(i)) {
                result[index] = i;
                index++;
                set.remove(i);
            }
        }
        return Arrays.copyOf(result, index);
    }
}
